  spriteInReoucesFolder:
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6e8415b70f2a34844811ba5849a4068b, type: 3}
  loadingSpriteInReoucesFolder:
  - com.zen.driving.car.midnight.club.splash.01
  message: {fileID: 453412243372740209}
  isToUpperCase: 0
  maxLenght: 120
  messages:
  - Brake before entering corners, then accelerate smoothly to maximize exit speed
    and grip.
  - Lean naturally through turns and avoid sudden steering inputs to maintain full
    control.
  - Focus your eyes far ahead on the track to react faster and choose the best racing
    line.
  - Use throttle control carefully when exiting corners to prevent wheel spin and
    instability.
  - Draft behind opponents on long straights to gain extra speed, then overtake just
    before the next braking zone.
  - Keep a smooth racing line through every bend to carry more speed and save valuable
    time.
  - Draft behind opponents on straight roads to gain speed before making an overtaking
    move.
  - Avoid excessive braking during races because momentum is often the key to faster
    laps.
  - Learn every track layout and corner sequence to predict hazards and improve consistency.
  - Balance speed and control in every situation because clean riding wins more races
    often.
